# Prettier exists in this repo for exactly ONE job: formatting the generated
# index.html so the committed build output is a stable fixed point (see
# package.json "build"). Everything else is explicitly out of scope, so that a
# stray `npx prettier --write .` is a complete no-op.
#
# Verify that property with:  npx prettier --list-different .   (expect no output)
#
# NOTE: index.html is deliberately NOT listed here - it is the one file Prettier is
# supposed to touch.

# --- not ours to reformat ---

# The 6 remaining Framer export pages.
/about.html
/donate.html
/films.html
/privacy-policy.html
/volunteer.html
/404.html

# The Framer export's stylesheet and the rest of the 20 MB asset tree. These are
# byte-exact migration output verified against the live site; reflowing them would
# produce a huge meaningless diff and could shift document height, which the layout
# work depends on being exact.
/assets/

# course.html is a committed standalone artifact from the codebase-to-course skill.
# Not deploy content, and far too large to be worth a reformat diff.
/course.html

# Hand-written markdown with deliberately wrapped tables and code fences.
# Prettier's markdown reflow would be a large unwanted diff.
/AGENTS.md
/README.md

# Long-form analysis docs, hand-written and heavily wrapped. Same reasoning as the
# markdown above.
/docs/

# Build inputs. Prettier has poor Nunjucks support and would mangle the tags, and
# the config here exists only to be read by the build.
/src/
/eleventy.config.mjs

# Generated.
/package-lock.json
node_modules/